{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2030","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. A TRUE Battle"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice and Bob are playing a game. There is a list of $$$n$$$ booleans, each of which is either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", given as a binary string $$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ of length $$$n$$$ (where $$$\\texttt{1}$$$ represents "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and $$$\\texttt{0}$$$ represents "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Initially, there are no operators between the booleans."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Alice and Bob will take alternate turns placing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" between the booleans, with Alice going first. Thus, the game will consist of $$$n-1$$$ turns since there are $$$n$$$ booleans. Alice aims for the final statement to evaluate to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", while Bob aims for it to evaluate to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Given the list of boolean values, determine whether Alice will win if both players play optimally."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"To evaluate the final expression, repeatedly perform the following steps until the statement consists of a single "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":": "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If the statement contains an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operator, choose any one and replace the subexpression surrounding it with its evaluation. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Otherwise, the statement contains an "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" operator. Choose any one and replace the subexpression surrounding the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with its evaluation. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"text","text":" For example, the expression "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true or false and false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is evaluated as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true or (false and false)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$=$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true or false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" $$$=$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". It can be shown that the result of any compound statement is unique."},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$A binary string is a string that only consists of characters $$$\\texttt{0}$$$ and $$$\\texttt{1}$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\leq t \\leq 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains an integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2 \\leq n \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the string."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a binary string of length $$$n$$$, consisting of characters $$$\\texttt{0}$$$ and $$$\\texttt{1}$$$ — the list of boolean values."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) if Alice wins, and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" in any case (for example, strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as a positive response)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n2\n11\n3\n010\n12\n101111111100\n10\n0111111011\n8\n01000010\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nYES\nYES\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase, Alice can place "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" between the two booleans. The game ends as there are no other places to place operators, and Alice wins because "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true and true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second testcase, Alice can place "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"or"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" between the middle "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the left "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". Bob can place "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"and"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" between the middle "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"true"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the right "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". The statement "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false or true and false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"false"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that these examples may not be the best strategies for either Alice or Bob."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"2030C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2030/problem/C"}